node_modules
dist

# Bench artifacts: cpuprofiles, generated mutants, captured baselines, bundled
# libraries. Large (tens of MB) and regenerated by `bench/` on demand — the
# scripts are tracked, their output is not. Every bench subdirectory writes to a
# `.out/` of its own (`bench/vs/.out/` holds the bundles the comparison builds),
# so the pattern covers the tree rather than just the root.
bench/**/.out/
# The documented profile command sends its output to `bench/.out/prof`, which the
# rule above already covers. This catches the run that omits `--cpu-prof-dir`:
# V8 then drops `CPU.<timestamp>.cpuprofile` into the working directory, which is
# usually the repo root and outside every bench rule.
*.cpuprofile

